WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Three tasks. Growing experience.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.284
Task 1: Observe the blocks and cups. Locate the red block and a suitable cup.

00:00:08.284 --> 00:00:27.060
Task 1: Cover red first. Grasp with the left arm; transport opening-down.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:47.106
Task 1: Continue the red cover. Preserve the grasp during transport.

00:00:47.106 --> 00:00:48.396
Task 1: Red cover complete. Release and withdraw from the cup.

00:00:48.396 --> 00:01:03.520
Task 1: Cover green next. Grasp the next cup with the right arm.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.652
Task 1: Clear the cup for transport. Lift along a clear path.

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:29.172
Task 1: Complete the green cover. Transport and lower opening-down.

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:30.348
Task 1: Green cover complete. Release and withdraw.

00:01:30.348 --> 00:01:53.062
Task 1: Cover blue last. Grasp the remaining cup with the left arm.

00:01:53.062 --> 00:02:16.750
Task 1: Complete the blue cover. Transport, lower and release the cup.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:16.833
Task 1: All three covers complete. Leave the cups stable.

00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:19.833
Task success verified.

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:24.833
Update knowledge. Carry it forward.

00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:27.357
Task 2: Read the displayed counts. Locate the buttons in the current scene.

00:02:27.357 --> 00:02:47.199
Task 2: Green: first of two presses. Approach above the cap with a closed gripper.

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:48.267
Task 2: Green: first cycle complete. Release and withdraw clear.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:03:05.935
Task 2: Green: second of two presses. Repeat one distinct contact-and-release cycle.

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:07.371
Task 2: Green count complete. Withdraw before switching targets.

00:03:07.371 --> 00:03:25.123
Task 2: Blue: one press. Ground the approach at the blue cap.

00:03:25.123 --> 00:03:26.027
Task 2: Blue count complete. Release and withdraw.

00:03:26.027 --> 00:03:44.159
Task 2: Red: confirm the entered counts. Press red once; release and withdraw.

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:44.903
Task 2: Confirmation complete. Leave the buttons clear.

00:03:44.903 --> 00:03:46.843
Task 2: Review the completed sequence. Observe the display and button states.

00:03:46.843 --> 00:03:47.873
Task 2: Check the current button states. Use a fresh observation.

00:03:47.873 --> 00:03:50.123
Task 2: Finish the task review. Reobserve the numbers and buttons.

00:03:50.123 --> 00:03:50.292
Task 2: Final observation complete. Keep the arms clear.

00:03:50.292 --> 00:03:53.292
Task success verified.

00:03:53.292 --> 00:03:58.292
Update knowledge. Carry it forward.

00:03:58.292 --> 00:04:00.590
Task 3: Reveal the hidden blocks. Locate the covering cup.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:16.706
Task 3: Uncover before counting. Grasp the cup with the left arm.

00:04:16.706 --> 00:04:24.652
Task 3: Refine the lift path. Preserve the grasp; update the lift motion.

00:04:24.652 --> 00:04:27.300
Task 3: The blocks are exposed. Hold the cup clear of the blocks.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:47.344
Task 3: Set the cup aside. Refresh placement bindings; choose support and clearance.

00:04:47.344 --> 00:04:52.824
Task 3: Clear the first arm. Leave the cup supported; withdraw the open gripper.

00:04:52.824 --> 00:05:05.600
Task 3: Prepare red ×2, green ×1, blue ×1. Approach red with the right arm; no contact yet.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.068
Task 3: Red approach reached. Prepare one distinct press-and-release cycle.

00:05:07.068 --> 00:05:22.138
Task 3: Red: first of two presses. Press once, release, then withdraw.

00:05:22.138 --> 00:05:23.324
Task 3: Red: first cycle complete. Keep the completed count.

00:05:23.324 --> 00:05:37.290
Task 3: Red: second of two presses. Complete a separate press-and-release cycle.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.628
Task 3: Red count complete. Withdraw before changing targets.

00:05:38.628 --> 00:05:45.504
Task 3: Re-ground the green target. Approach without contact.

00:05:45.504 --> 00:05:47.702
Task 3: Green approach reached. Stay above the button without pressing.

00:05:47.702 --> 00:05:49.854
Task 3: Refresh the green-button binding. Identify the cap and update its geometry.

00:05:49.854 --> 00:06:11.268
Task 3: Green: one press. Use the refreshed geometry; press and release.

00:06:11.268 --> 00:06:12.354
Task 3: Green cycle complete. Withdraw with the gripper closed.

00:06:12.354 --> 00:06:25.522
Task 3: Blue: one press. Ground the blue-cap approach; press and release.

00:06:25.522 --> 00:06:33.546
Task 3: Complete the blue cycle. Withdraw to clear the blue cap.

00:06:33.546 --> 00:06:35.202
Task 3: Review the composed task. Keep both arms clear.

00:06:35.202 --> 00:06:38.520
Task 3: Review the existing blue cycle. Use the current view and prior contact evidence.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.008
Task 3: Continue the final task check. Reobserve without contact.

00:06:40.008 --> 00:06:42.080
Task 3: Resolve the final task assessment. Hold both arms clear.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:42.375
Task 3: Finish the task review. Reobserve the button workspace.

00:06:42.375 --> 00:06:45.375
Task success verified.

00:06:45.375 --> 00:06:51.375
Turn physical experience into reusable knowledge.

